/*
================================================================================
 Memorizer API - test data
================================================================================

 Ready-made rows for an EMPTY (already migrated) Memorizer database: plain
 INSERT statements only, no generation logic. Run the whole file as a single
 batch (no GO separators are used).

 The questionnaires hold real subject matter - languages, programming, science,
 geography, the arts and practical skills - so a training session can actually
 be worked through rather than just counted.

 Contents
 --------
       6 users                    -> [dbo].[AspNetUsers], [memorizer].[rUserActivity]
      50 questionnaires           -> [memorizer].[rQuestionnaire]
         (20 private, 30 public, 7 removed)
    2500 questions               -> [memorizer].[rQuestion]
         (50 per questionnaire, removed questionnaires included; 100 removed)
    1946 typed answers           -> [memorizer].[rTypedAnswer]
         (68 removed)
    1500 question statuses       -> [memorizer].[nnQuestionUser]
         (499 new, 587 with penalty points)
      12 trainings               -> [memorizer].[rTraining]
         (6 by questions count, 6 by time, 2 removed)
      36 training questionnaires -> [memorizer].[nnTrainingQuestionnaire]

 Tables with the "j" prefix (jEventLog, jTrainingResult, jTrainingResultTypedAnswer,
 jAuthenticationCache), sLabel and nnEntityLabel are intentionally left empty.

 Question types
 --------------
 Following SkorpFiles.Memorizer.Api.Models.Enums.QuestionType:

   1  Task                    a task with nothing to check: sing it, go and do
                              it, look it up. No answer of either kind.
   2  UntypedAnswer           an answer to be spoken aloud, held in
                              [QuestionUntypedAnswer]. No typed answers.
   3  UntypedAndTypedAnswers  both: the answer is spoken first, then the key
                              words are typed. [QuestionUntypedAnswer] is
                              filled AND there are rows in [rTypedAnswer].
   4  TypedAnswers            short answers to be typed, held in
                              [rTypedAnswer]. [QuestionUntypedAnswer] is NULL.

 Test accounts
 -------------
 The password hashes are real ASP.NET Core Identity V3 hashes (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512,
 100000 iterations), so POST /Account/Token works out of the box. Log in with the
 LOGIN column - the API resolves users by user name, not by e-mail.

   login   | password    | e-mail                | owns
   --------+-------------+-----------------------+-----------------------------------
   alice   | Alice@2026  | alice@memorizer.test  | 8 questionnaires
   bob     | Bob@2026!   | bob@memorizer.test    | 8 questionnaires
   carol   | Carol@2026  | carol@memorizer.test  | 9 questionnaires
   dave    | Dave@2026!  | dave@memorizer.test   | 8 questionnaires
   erin    | Erin@2026!  | erin@memorizer.test   | 9 questionnaires
   frank   | Frank@2026  | frank@memorizer.test  | 8 questionnaires

 Questionnaires
 --------------
