    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001023', 4, N'What process builds a protein from messenger RNA?', NULL, 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 23, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001024', 4, N'What is a group of three RNA bases coding for an amino acid called?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 24, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001025', 4, N'Who described the double helix with Francis Crick in 1953?', NULL, 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 25, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-07T09:00:00'),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001026', 2, N'Explain the difference between a prokaryotic and a eukaryotic cell.', N'A prokaryote has no nucleus and no membrane-bound organelles; a eukaryote keeps its DNA in a nucleus and has specialised compartments.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 1, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 26, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001027', 2, N'Explain the central dogma of molecular biology.', N'Information flows from DNA to RNA to protein: the gene is transcribed and the transcript is translated.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 27, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001028', 2, N'Explain the difference between mitosis and meiosis.', N'Mitosis makes two identical cells for growth and repair; meiosis makes four cells with half the chromosomes, for reproduction.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 28, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001029', 2, N'Explain what a dominant and a recessive allele mean.', N'A dominant allele shows its effect with only one copy; a recessive one needs both copies to be visible.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 29, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001030', 2, N'Explain why DNA replication is called semi-conservative.', N'Each new molecule keeps one original strand and one newly built one.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 30, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001031', 2, N'Explain what a mutation is and why not all of them matter.', N'A change in the sequence; many fall in unused regions or code for the same amino acid, so nothing changes.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 31, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001032', 2, N'Explain what mitochondria have to do with maternal inheritance.', N'They carry their own small genome and are passed on almost entirely in the egg, so that DNA traces the maternal line.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 32, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001033', 2, N'Explain what enzymes do to a reaction.', N'They lower the activation energy and speed it enormously, without being used up themselves.', 1, NULL, 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 33, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001034', 2, N'Explain what osmosis is.', N'Water moves across a semi-permeable membrane towards the side with the higher concentration of dissolved substances.', 0, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 34, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001035', 2, N'Explain what stem cells are and why they matter.', N'Unspecialised cells that can divide and become several cell types, which makes repair and development possible.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 35, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001036', 3, N'What does CRISPR allow, and where did it come from?', N'Precise editing of DNA at a chosen site; it was found as a bacterial defence against viruses.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 36, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001037', 3, N'What is a plasmid, and why is it useful in the laboratory?', N'A small circular DNA molecule separate from the chromosome, used to carry genes into bacteria.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 37, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001038', 3, N'What is PCR used for?', N'Copying a chosen stretch of DNA millions of times so that there is enough to analyse.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 38, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001039', 3, N'What are telomeres, and what happens to them over time?', N'Repeated caps on the ends of chromosomes that shorten with each division, limiting how often a cell divides.', 1, NULL, 1, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 39, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001040', 3, N'What is apoptosis?', N'Programmed cell death, by which the body removes damaged or unneeded cells in an orderly way.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 40, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001041', 3, N'What is the difference between DNA and RNA, in three points?', N'RNA has ribose rather than deoxyribose, uracil rather than thymine, and is usually single-stranded.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 41, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001042', 3, N'What does a ribosome read, and what does it produce?', N'It reads messenger RNA in codons and links amino acids into a protein chain.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 42, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001043', 3, N'What is an operon, and in which kind of organism is it found?', N'A cluster of genes under one promoter, switched on together; it is typical of bacteria.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 43, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001044', 3, N'What does "haploid" mean, and which human cells are haploid?', N'Carrying one set of chromosomes; sperm and egg cells are haploid.', 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 44, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001045', 1, N'Draw a labelled diagram of an animal cell from memory and check it.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 45, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001046', 1, N'Look at pond water under a microscope and name what you can see.', NULL, 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 240, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 46, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001047', 1, N'Work out a Punnett square for two heterozygous parents and predict the ratios.', NULL, 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 300, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 47, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001048', 1, N'Extract DNA from a strawberry with washing-up liquid, salt and alcohol.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 360, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 48, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001049', 1, N'Read a news article about gene editing and explain the science in it aloud.', NULL, 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 420, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 49, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001050', 1, N'Explain to someone why identical twins are not truly identical.', NULL, 1, N'Wikipedia: Cell biology', 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 50, '2026-02-02T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-07T09:00:00');

-- 22. Weather and clouds (public, owner: carol)
     QuestionIsFixed, QuestionEstimatedTrainingTimeSeconds, QuestionnaireId, QuestionQuestionnaireCode,
     ObjectCreationTime, ObjectIsRemoved, ObjectRemovalTime)
VALUES
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001051', 4, N'What is the name of the high, wispy ice cloud?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 1, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001052', 4, N'What is the name of the low, lumpy sheet cloud?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 2, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001053', 4, N'What is the name of the flat, featureless low cloud layer?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 3, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001054', 4, N'What is the name of the tall storm cloud with an anvil top?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 4, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001055', 4, N'What is the name of the fair-weather heap cloud?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 5, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001056', 4, N'What is the name of the mid-level layered cloud?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 6, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001057', 4, N'What is the name of the rain-bearing grey layer?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 7, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001058', 4, N'What instrument measures atmospheric pressure?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 8, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001059', 4, N'What instrument measures wind speed?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 9, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001060', 4, N'What instrument measures humidity?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 10, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001061', 4, N'What instrument measures rainfall?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 11, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001062', 4, N'What is the SI unit used for atmospheric pressure on weather charts?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 12, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001063', 4, N'What is a line of equal pressure on a chart called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 1, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 13, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001064', 4, N'What is the boundary between two air masses called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 14, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001065', 4, N'What is a rotating column of air touching the ground called?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 15, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001066', 4, N'What is a tropical storm in the Atlantic called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 16, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001067', 4, N'What is the same storm called in the western Pacific?', NULL, 0, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 17, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001068', 4, N'What is the layer of the atmosphere we live in called?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 18, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001069', 4, N'Which layer contains the ozone layer?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 19, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001070', 4, N'What is the temperature at which air becomes saturated called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 20, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001071', 4, N'What is frozen rain falling as pellets from a thunderstorm called?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 21, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001072', 4, N'What is the scale used for tornado strength called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 22, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001073', 4, N'What is the scale used for hurricane strength called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 23, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001074', 4, N'What is the name for wind blowing from the sea to the land during the day?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 24, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001075', 4, N'What is a cloud that forms at ground level called?', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 25, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-08T09:00:00'),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001076', 2, N'Explain how clouds form.', N'Moist air rises, cools to its dew point and the water vapour condenses onto tiny particles into droplets.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 1, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 26, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001077', 2, N'Explain the difference between a warm front and a cold front.', N'A warm front slides gently over cooler air, bringing long steady rain; a cold front undercuts warm air steeply, bringing short heavy showers.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 27, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001078', 2, N'Explain why it is colder at the top of a mountain.', N'Air expands and cools as pressure falls with height, and the ground that warms the air is far below.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 28, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001079', 2, N'Explain how a thunderstorm produces lightning.', N'Ice and water particles collide inside the cloud and separate charge, until the difference is large enough to break down the air.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 29, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001080', 2, N'Explain why you see lightning before you hear thunder.', N'Light reaches you almost instantly; sound takes about three seconds per kilometre.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 30, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001081', 2, N'Explain what relative humidity means.', N'How much water vapour the air holds as a percentage of the most it could hold at that temperature.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 31, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001082', 2, N'Explain what causes wind.', N'Air moves from higher to lower pressure, deflected by the rotation of the Earth.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 32, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001083', 2, N'Explain what the jet stream is and why forecasters watch it.', N'A fast ribbon of wind high in the atmosphere that steers the depressions and separates warm from cold air.', 1, NULL, 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 33, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001084', 2, N'Explain why weather forecasts lose accuracy after about a week.', N'The atmosphere is chaotic, so tiny errors in the starting state grow quickly into large differences.', 0, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 34, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001085', 2, N'Explain the difference between weather and climate.', N'Weather is the state of the atmosphere now; climate is the statistics of weather over decades.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 35, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001086', 3, N'What does a cumulonimbus cloud bring, and what shape marks a mature one?', N'Heavy showers, hail, lightning and gusts; the flattened anvil top marks it.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 36, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001087', 3, N'What are lenticular clouds, and where do they form?', N'Smooth lens-shaped clouds that hang downwind of mountains in a standing wave.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 37, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001088', 3, N'What is a mackerel sky made of?', N'Rows of small cirrocumulus or altocumulus, often a sign of approaching change.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 38, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001089', 3, N'What causes a rainbow, and where must the Sun be?', N'Sunlight refracted and reflected inside raindrops, with the Sun behind the observer.', 1, NULL, 1, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 39, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001090', 3, N'What is a halo around the Sun or Moon caused by?', N'Ice crystals in high cirrus cloud bending the light through twenty-two degrees.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 40, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001091', 3, N'What is the difference between sleet and freezing rain?', N'Sleet freezes into pellets on the way down; freezing rain stays liquid and turns to ice on contact.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 41, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001092', 3, N'What is the eye of a hurricane, and what is it like inside?', N'A calm clear centre where air sinks, ringed by the strongest winds in the eyewall.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 42, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001093', 3, N'What is a microburst and why is it dangerous to aircraft?', N'A small violent downdraught that spreads out at the ground, changing the wind sharply on approach.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 43, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001094', 3, N'What is the Coriolis effect and which way does it deflect in the north?', N'The deflection caused by the Earth''s rotation; it turns moving air to the right in the northern hemisphere.', 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 44, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001095', 1, N'Photograph the sky each day for a week and name the cloud type in every picture.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 45, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001096', 1, N'Read a synoptic chart and describe out loud what weather it predicts.', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 240, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 46, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001097', 1, N'Measure the temperature and pressure at home for five days and plot both.', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 300, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 47, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001098', 1, N'Count the seconds between lightning and thunder and work out the distance.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 360, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 48, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001099', 1, N'Compare three forecasts for the same day and see which was closest.', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 420, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 49, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001100', 1, N'Explain the water cycle aloud without using notes.', NULL, 1, N'World Meteorological Organization: cloud atlas', 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000022', 50, '2026-02-03T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-08T09:00:00');

