    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001620', 4, N'Which strait separates England from France?', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 20, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001621', 4, N'Which current warms north-western Europe?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 21, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001622', 4, N'What is the name for a very large wave caused by an earthquake?', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 25, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 22, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001623', 4, N'What is the average salinity of sea water, roughly, in parts per thousand?', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 30, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 23, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001624', 4, N'What is the largest coral reef system called?', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 15, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 24, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001625', 4, N'What is the name for the shallow shelf around a continent?', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 20, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 25, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-19T09:00:00'),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001626', 2, N'Explain what causes ocean tides.', N'The gravitational pull of the Moon and, less strongly, the Sun, combined with the Earth''s rotation.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 1, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 26, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001627', 2, N'Explain the difference between a spring tide and a neap tide.', N'A spring tide comes when Sun and Moon pull in line and the range is largest; a neap tide when they pull at right angles and the range is least.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 27, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001628', 2, N'Explain what the thermohaline circulation is.', N'A slow global overturning driven by differences in temperature and salt, which carries heat between the hemispheres.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 28, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001629', 2, N'Explain why the sea is salty.', N'Rivers carry dissolved minerals from rock into the ocean, and evaporation leaves the salt behind.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 29, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001630', 2, N'Explain what ocean acidification is and what causes it.', N'Carbon dioxide dissolving into sea water lowers its pH, which makes it harder for shell-forming creatures to build their shells.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 30, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001631', 2, N'Explain what El Nino is.', N'A periodic warming of the eastern tropical Pacific that shifts rainfall and storm patterns across much of the world.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 31, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001632', 2, N'Explain how a tsunami differs from a wind-driven wave.', N'It is generated by the sudden displacement of the whole water column, so it carries enormous energy and long wavelength rather than surface motion.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 32, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001633', 2, N'Explain what the abyssal plain is.', N'The flat deep ocean floor beyond the continental slope, covered in fine sediment and lying several kilometres down.', 1, NULL, 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 33, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001634', 2, N'Explain what a hydrothermal vent is and why it is remarkable.', N'A crack on the sea floor venting hot mineral-rich water, supporting life that draws energy from chemistry rather than sunlight.', 0, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 34, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001635', 2, N'Explain why sea level is rising.', N'Water expands as it warms, and ice on land is melting into the sea.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 35, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001636', 3, N'How deep is the Mariana Trench, roughly, and what is its deepest point called?', N'About eleven kilometres, at Challenger Deep.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 36, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001637', 3, N'Which sea has no coastline, and what defines it?', N'The Sargasso Sea, bounded by ocean currents rather than land.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 37, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001638', 3, N'Which is the largest inland body of water, and is it a sea or a lake?', N'The Caspian, a salt lake usually called a sea.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 38, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001639', 3, N'What is the Great Pacific Garbage Patch?', N'A vast area where currents concentrate floating plastic, mostly as small fragments rather than a solid raft.', 1, NULL, 1, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 39, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001640', 3, N'What does the Coriolis effect do to ocean currents?', N'It deflects them, so gyres turn clockwise in the north and anticlockwise in the south.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 40, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001641', 3, N'What is the halocline?', N'The layer where salinity changes sharply with depth.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 41, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001642', 3, N'What is upwelling, and why are those waters rich in fish?', N'Wind drives surface water away and deep water rises, bringing nutrients that feed plankton and the food chain above it.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 42, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001643', 3, N'What is the difference between a sea and a gulf?', N'A sea is a large body partly enclosed by land; a gulf is a deep inlet of a sea or ocean with a narrower opening.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 43, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001644', 3, N'What is the Mid-Atlantic Ridge?', N'An underwater mountain chain where the plates spread apart and new crust forms, running the length of the Atlantic.', 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 44, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001645', 1, N'Trace the world''s five oceans and ten major seas on a blank map.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 45, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001646', 1, N'Find the tide table for a coast you know and predict tomorrow''s high tide.', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 240, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 46, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001647', 1, N'Read about one deep-sea creature and describe how it survives the pressure.', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 300, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 47, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001648', 1, N'Follow a shipping route on a live tracking site and name the seas it crosses.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 360, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 48, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001649', 1, N'Compare the depth of the Mariana Trench with the height of Everest on paper.', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 420, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 49, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001650', 1, N'Explain to someone why the sea is salty.', NULL, 1, N'The Times Atlas of the Oceans', 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 50, '2026-02-14T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-19T09:00:00');

