    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001826', 2, N'Explain what a bildungsroman is and give an example.', N'A novel following a character''s growth from youth to maturity, such as Great Expectations.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 1, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 26, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001827', 2, N'Explain what stream of consciousness is and who used it.', N'A narration following thought as it runs, without tidy ordering, used by Joyce and Woolf.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 27, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001828', 2, N'Explain what an unreliable narrator is.', N'A narrator whose account cannot be taken at face value, so the reader must work out what really happened.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 28, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001829', 2, N'Explain what magical realism is.', N'A style in which impossible events appear in an otherwise realistic setting and are told matter-of-factly.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 29, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001830', 2, N'Explain the difference between a novel and a novella.', N'Length and scope: a novella is shorter and usually holds to a single line of action.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 30, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001831', 2, N'Explain what the epistolary form is and name a novel that uses it.', N'A story told through letters or documents, as Dracula and the early parts of Frankenstein are.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 31, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001832', 2, N'Explain what a dystopia is and how it differs from a utopia.', N'A dystopia imagines a society organised badly, often by the very means meant to perfect it; a utopia imagines one organised well.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 45, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 32, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001833', 2, N'Explain what modernism did to the novel.', N'It broke with linear plot and settled narration, turning attention to consciousness, fragmentation and the surface of language.', 1, NULL, 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 33, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001834', 2, N'Explain what a frame narrative is, with an example.', N'A story told inside another story, as in Wuthering Heights, where a tenant records a housekeeper''s account.', 0, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 34, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001835', 2, N'Explain why translations of the same novel can differ so much.', N'The translator makes constant choices about register, rhythm and idiom, and every choice shapes the voice the reader hears.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 35, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001836', 3, N'Which novel opens with a line about a truth universally acknowledged?', N'Pride and Prejudice by Jane Austen.', 1, NULL, 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 36, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001837', 3, N'Which novel opens with a man waking as an insect, and what is the story called?', N'The Metamorphosis by Kafka - a novella rather than a novel.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 37, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001838', 3, N'Which novel is set on a whaling ship pursuing a white whale?', N'Moby-Dick by Melville.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 38, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001839', 3, N'Which novel invented the word "Big Brother"?', N'Nineteen Eighty-Four by Orwell.', 1, NULL, 1, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 39, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001840', 3, N'Which novel follows one day in Dublin, and on what date?', N'Ulysses, set on the sixteenth of June 1904.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 60, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 40, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001841', 3, N'Which novel begins with a family of seven generations in Macondo?', N'One Hundred Years of Solitude.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 75, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 41, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001842', 3, N'Which Russian novel opens with a line about happy and unhappy families?', N'Anna Karenina by Tolstoy.', 1, NULL, 0, 90, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 42, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001843', 3, N'Which novel was the first to win the Booker Prize twice for its author, and who?', N'Several authors have won twice; Hilary Mantel did so with Wolf Hall and Bring Up the Bodies.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 105, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 43, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001844', 3, N'Which novel is narrated by Death?', N'The Book Thief by Markus Zusak.', 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 120, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 44, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001845', 1, N'Read the first page of five novels you have never opened and choose one to finish.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 45, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001846', 1, N'Reread a novel you last read ten years ago and note what changed.', NULL, 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 240, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 46, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001847', 1, N'Learn the opening line of five famous novels and say them from memory.', NULL, 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 300, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 47, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001848', 1, N'Write a one-paragraph summary of the last novel you read, without notes.', NULL, 1, NULL, 0, 360, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 48, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001849', 1, N'Compare two translations of the same passage and say which you prefer and why.', NULL, 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 420, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 49, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 0, NULL),
    (N'B0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000001850', 1, N'Explain to someone why a novel you love is worth their time.', NULL, 1, N'The Penguin Companion to Literature', 0, 180, N'A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 50, '2026-02-18T09:00:00', 1, '2026-07-23T09:00:00');

